## ESMAI Letter Template
- **File:** `src/lib/esmai-letter-template.ts`
- **Purpose:** Official correspondence template for ESMAI (Environmental & Spatial Meteorology AI), a project of Aetheris Vision LLC.
- **Usage:** `import { buildEsmaiLetter, buildSalutation, buildClosing } from '@/lib/esmai-letter-template'`
- **Returns:** Self-contained, print-ready HTML string — compatible with DocuSeal (`includeSignatureFields: true`) and direct PDF/print rendering.
- **Key options:** `recipientName`, `recipientOrg`, `recipientAddress[]`, `subject`, `body` (HTML), `referenceNumber`, `date`, `appendSignature`, `includeSignatureFields`.
- **When to use:** Any formal client communication — SLAs, proposals, engagement letters, white-paper cover letters, or invoices needing letterhead.
- **Brand:** ESMAI navy/sky-blue palette (`#0f172a` / `#0ea5e9`), Inter font, Aetheris Vision LLC as parent entity, Marston Ward as signatory.
- **Stored SLAs:** `src/data/sla-*.html` — pre-rendered letters for specific clients (e.g., `sla-tropical-hut.html`).

## Coding Rules
- TypeScript strict — never use `any`
- App Router patterns only — no Pages Router patterns
- Server Components by default — use `"use client"` only when necessary
- Always use SSH git remote (never HTTPS)
- Env vars: never hardcode secrets — all in Vercel environment variables
- No console.log in production code — use proper error handling
